{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C#]The [D#m]old man sleeps in Moab and the forty years are through
The [C#]servant of the LORD is gone, the [B]people look to you
The [D#m]Jordan's rolling wide ahead, the far bank out of sight
[C#]And Joshua son of Nun stands listening [B]at the river's side
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[C#]Moses my servant [B]is dead
Now get [C#]up and cross this Jordan [B]
As I [C#]was with Moses, so I will [D#m]be with you
[B]I will not fail [C#]you or forsake you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]Have I not commanded [F#]you
Be strong and courageous
[C#]Do not be terrified or [B]dismayed
For [D#m]the LORD your God [F#]is with you [C#]wherever you [D#m]go
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C#]Keep [D#m]the law upon your lips and think on it by day and night
[C#]Never turning from the road to the [B]left hand or the right
When the [D#m]walls ahead are high and your knees begin to shake
Re[C#]member who has spoken and [B]the promise he won't [C#]break
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Moses my servant [B]is dead
Now get [C#]up and cross this Jordan [B]
As I [C#]was with Moses, so I will [D#m]be with you
I [B]will not fail you [C#]or forsake you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]Have I not commanded you
[F#]Be strong and courageous
[C#]Do not be terrified or dis[B]mayed
For the LORD [D#m]your God is with [F#]you wherever you [C#]go
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Every place where [B]the sole [D#m]of your foot treads I have given you
No [F#]one will be able [C#]to stand against you
Be strong and very [B]courageous [D#m][B][D#m][F#]
[C#]Be strong and very courageous
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The LORD [C#]your God is with you wherever you go
{end_of_verse}

